   "he": "מִי שֶׁחֶצְיוֹ עֶבֶד וְחֶצְיוֹ בֶּן חוֹרִין לֹא יֹאכַל מִשֶּׁל רַבּוֹ וְכוּ׳. מִשֶּׁל רַבּוֹ הוּא דְּלֹא יֹאכַל, אֲבָל מִשֶּׁל עַצְמוֹ — יֹאכַל. וְהָא תַּנְיָא: לֹא יֹאכַל לֹא מִשֶּׁלּוֹ וְלֹא מִשֶּׁל רַבּוֹ.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «One who is half slave and half free man may not eat from his master’s» Paschal lamb. It is specifically «from his master’s» lamb that «he may not eat; however, from his own» lamb «he may eat. But wasn’t it taught» in a baraita: He «may eat neither from his own nor from his master’s» Paschal lamb?"
  }
